# Copy this file to .env and fill in the one blank at the bottom.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THROWAWAY KEYS. EVERY SECRET BELOW IS PUBLIC AND WORTHLESS.
#
# All three keypairs are committed to this repository, so anybody who has read it can be the
# agent, be Alice and be Bob. They are here so that `docker compose up` is the whole setup and
# nobody generates a key before they can see anything. Carrying one of them into a real
# deployment hands your agent's identity to every reader of this file.
#
# Generate your own with `nak key generate`, or in Node with `nostr-tools`:
#   generateSecretKey() -> 32 bytes; getPublicKey(sk) -> 64 lowercase hex characters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Shared Agent's own keypair. `main.ts` reads the secret and decodes it to 32 raw bytes
# itself, the framework parsing no key material. The public key is what a person writes to; it
# is derived from the secret, and it is stated here only because the `nak` containers need it
# and must never be given the secret it comes from.
NOSTR_AGENT_SECRET_KEY=290db7358191556e1a405bd4f68a3424cc234480feff4b550e8ff2e8eb95b242
NOSTR_AGENT_PUBKEY=4cff13c02e50b29f1d36406c74b5dfdbe5b121e27690dcfabc45539952972769

# The two people. `main.ts` reads the two public keys and never the secrets: an Operator records
# a public key they were handed out of band, and the secret stays with the person. Here each
# secret goes to that person's own `nak` container and nowhere else.
ALICE_PUBKEY=4b73103953d4c174542765b35096f6de5da77f7267125a210e1e8daa5cf8d1b0
ALICE_SECRET_KEY=0bcf3926e2f18ffc45b320ddeb62b1a381cc4f2976a7c9419df9e59d82023a7c

BOB_PUBKEY=2494a91386d05876a2a647658c968ddba2abc5691e18907cbf4920176179e0f0
BOB_SECRET_KEY=68ca172039e733959e11b8156fbca7a93afeed97307b5a1123bcce7c2c635fea
